<title>HONG KONG: China Merchants Hai Hong 1996 net higher.</title>
<headline>China Merchants Hai Hong 1996 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   22.5	 vs  14.6</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs  6.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  54.86 gain vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    158.73     vs  103.02</p>
<p>    Turnover		     802.38     vs  890.93</p>
<p>    Company name		 China Merchants Hai Hong Holdings</p>
<p>				     Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE -  China Merchants Hai Hong is a paint manufacturer.</p>
<p>The exceptional item represents a gain on disposal of a 4.95 percent interest in Ming Wah Universal (Bermuda) Co Ltd (Ming Wah) and a gain arising on the dilution of the group's shareholding to 75 percent of the enlarged issued share capital of Ming Wah, following the listing of the shares of Ming Wah, which owns and operates a fleet of vessels, on the Stock Exchange of Singapore.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is two H.K. cents (including interim dividend of two cents) vs nine cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
